        {
          "type": "tool",
          "data": {
            "content": "[{\"namespace\":[\"memories\",\"baseline-run1-f5454b\"],\"key\":\"4c4ad402-9dbb-4ad4-ad99-88970eba082b\",\"value\":{\"content\":\"Qdrant is a dedicated vector database written in Rust. Deployment: Self-hostable (Apache 2.0) as a single binary or via Docker/K8s. Managed cloud also available. Memory optimization: Binary quantization reduces RAM usage up to 32x with a modest recall hit (recovered via oversampling + rescoring). In our test it cut a 24GB deployment to under 2GB of hot RAM. Performance: p95 ~12ms at 10M vectors with 97% recall. Strong filtered-search performance with payload indexes. Operational notes: New service to run: monitoring, upgrades, snapshots are all new surface. Snapshot/restore tooling is solid. Team has no prior Rust-service operational experience, though none is strictly required.\"},\"created_at\":\"2026-08-12T01:25:20.837386+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-12T01:25:20.837386+00:00\",\"score\":0.6864302905964939}]",
